# Hand-written PDBx/mmCIF, not an archive entry.
#
# What it demonstrates: two alternate conformers of one serine, A and B, differing in OG.  Both
# conformers must survive as distinct atoms, and no bond may ever join conformer A to conformer B --
# alternate conformers are alternative descriptions of one place, and treating them as coexisting
# atoms is what gave chython 2's geometric perception 89 spurious cross-residue bonds on one entry.
#
# The backbone atoms carry no alt id, so they belong to both conformers and bond to either.
# Expected: 8 atoms; CB-OG built twice (A-A and B-B) and never crosswise.
data_TESTALT
_entry.id   TESTALT
#
loop_
_chem_comp_bond.comp_id
_chem_comp_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_comp_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_comp_bond.value_order
SER N  CA SING
SER CA C  SING
SER C  O  DOUB
SER CA CB SING
SER CB OG SING
#
